 rule book for this  everyone's going through it for the  first time so  i reached out to several coaches and got  their opinion and  um like coach izzo can't thank him  enough for his help and his  his ideas but uh most people said it's  gonna take you  uh two weeks it's gonna take you uh four  games to get back to normal  when we came back we played six games 14  days  traveled 3 500 miles so you were just  playing prepping recovering  and we never got the practice in and  then once we  lost in our big 12 tournament we were  able to practice for the first time and  dan i mean you you gotta i don't care  what sport if you go off  and all of a sudden you don't putt for  21 days and then you say go out and putt  you're not gonna be a good putter  so we actually had to practice and get  back to old habits defensively of what  we do and how we do it and then  that really was a blessing that enabled  us to go on our run in the ncaa  tournament  yeah but it's tricky because i don't  know if you thought the  season could be in jeopardy here i mean  that's it pretty severe i don't know  did you feel that way no no no no  definitely you  with with kobet there are no uh absolute  answers and i didn't know  maybe we don't come back in time and uh  maybe we can't get back to where we were  because  for most of season we were top three  offenses in the country and top three  defenses in the country  so analytically we were really sound but  when we came back our defense  every game we played dropped and we got  as low as 44th best defense in the  in the country and then all of a sudden  um after we had those couple times of  practice and really credit our guys when  we practice  they practice hard they wanted to get  better it's a player-led team  and put in time you're you know you're  just trying to get by  and our guys wanted to get better he's  uh scott drew the head coach at baylor's  been there since 2003.  you know you go back you took over a  program that  like you know i think people wonder if  they were going to get the death penalty  if that was going to happen with the  ncaa and  even when uh you know you it took a  little while to get to the tournament  you had some rough losses there i think  yale and georgia state and like if i  would have told you in 2003  scott one day we're going to talk about  you winning a national championship at  baylor and you would have said  i said yeah i i definitely see us doing  it i would have probably thought it  would have been sooner than 18 years  because when you're younger  you just assume things are easier you  know but we went to 28 in 2010  lost to the national champ and i thought  we could have won it that year we lost  it 2012 to the national champion the  elite eight  um so i mean we're knocking on the door  um  since 2008 only us in kansas and the  power five have won 18 or more games in  the last three out of five seasons we've  been ranked number one so we've been  close  and uh um uh i know when you're close  and don't get something  you're that much more appreciative when  you do achieve it i wondered at half  time though  because gonzaga cut it to ten yes and  there was momentum  on gonzaga's part and look like your  guys were arguing a little bit  and seemed like you know you looked up  and you said we're only up by ten  what did you tell your team at halftime  well we're  first and foremost we're up ten we're 20  minutes away from a national  championship  so uh um but when you're up 19 you want  to go in and a half up 19 not up 10.  but they're a great team they're going  to make a run they're going to make  coaching adjustments but i think  focusing on the big picture  and the big pictures were up 10 and  we're 20 minutes away from a national  championship  and uh davion mitchell has hired an  agent so he's going to go pro  uh we're going to talk to those guys in  the next couple days but obviously uh  davion was unbelievable in the in the  tournament and  um uh him and jared uh all  tournament teams and really uh came back  and accomplished  what they set out to accomplish yeah i  don't mean to break this to you but uh  this is what uh breaking news now just  said that uh  mitchell a potential lottery pick  declaring for the draft and plans on  hiring an agent  sources tell the athletics so yeah no no  i know i i just know like before a  formal release okay  yeah we we'd coordinate that probably  you're right everything happens on  social media nowadays yes it does yes it  does  sometimes before the coach even knows  yeah uh  your brother is the head coach at grand  canyon bryce  uh are you going to schedule grand  canyon  um it's much easier to cheer for him  than play against him so we  prefer to play in the ncaa tournament in  the final four rather than playing home  and home and homes  oh come on you got to help out bryce a  little bit come on  well if that if that's something that  that that he ever needs uh um  obviously uh it's business too so you  got to do what's best for uh uh  on the business side but uh obviously  love my brother love gcu so happy for  them  first uh ncaa appearance first  conference tournament  uh championship first conference  championship so a lot of  a lot of successful things and a lot of  great things by their program and headed  in the right direction  uh congrats scott it's been a long time  it's like uh  you know you're became an overnight  sensation after 20 years  you know well i it's it's a tribute to  all our past players that helped us get  here  administration fan support uh and god's  really blessed our program  thank you scott and uh we appreciate  your time congrats  thank you dan thanks for all you do for  sports that's scott drew uh  doesn't look like he just turned 50 but  usually coaching will make you look like  you're about 60 or something but uh  congrats to baylor

